# HeroLower v21 — underside coverage preview

Built-in image generation edited the independent grayscale opacity mask.

Prompt direction: preserve the original polar layout and opaque inward-facing crowns. Replace uniform hero underside fade with unequal broad density lobes separated by softer dissolving gaps. On the upper-right diagonal bank, the southwest boundary faces the UV center and must remain crisp; only the northeast outward boundary fades. Preserve distant cloud banks. No shading, outlines, repeated fingers, or internal gray patches in the opaque core.

The first generated mask reversed the upper-right boundary and was rejected. Generated_Coverage.png is the corrected result.

Packaging uses the unchanged v15 RGB channels and fixed UV fit. Generated opacity is blended at 80% only inside selected partially transparent hero regions; fully opaque crowns remain identical. Source generation is 1254 square, packed texture is upscaled to 4096 square.

Applied asset: /Game/RXSkySystem/Cubeless/PaintedCloud/v04/Altitude/HeroLower_v21/T_CloudLook_HeroLower_v21

Applied to the current actor in /Temp/Untitled_1. The texture asset is saved; the untitled level remains unsaved. CloudCompositeBlend remains 0. This is a review candidate, not catalog approval.
